This distribution is Idha.NPoco, an unofficial fork maintained by Idha:

    https://github.com/idhase/NPoco

It is not affiliated with, nor endorsed by, the NPoco project. The assembly is
still named NPoco.dll, so Idha.NPoco cannot be installed alongside the official
NPoco package.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modifications to files from the upstream project
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This release changes two upstream files, adding 20 lines and widening three method
signatures. No upstream code is removed or rewritten.

src/NPoco/Expressions/SqlExpression.cs

    Widened FlattenList from private to protected, and FormatParameters and
    BuildInStatement from private to protected virtual, so that a
    database-specific expression can override IN clause generation. Added a
    protected GetColumnType helper. None of this changes behaviour.

    Added a branch to VisitBinary that wraps a DateTime compared against a
    LegacyDateTime column, mirroring the AnsiString branch immediately above
    it. This branch is reachable only for a column declared as LegacyDateTime,
    a type that does not exist upstream.

src/NPoco.FluentSql/SqlExpressionTranslator.cs

    Added the same LegacyDateTime wrap to Parameter, next to the existing
    AnsiString wrap, so FluentSql and the LINQ provider agree. Reachable only
    for a column declared as LegacyDateTime.

Earlier fork releases also diverge from upstream in these files:

    src/NPoco/NPoco.csproj
    src/NPoco.SqlServer/NPoco.SqlServer.csproj
    src/NPoco.SqlServer.SystemData/NPoco.SqlServer.SystemData.csproj
    test/NPoco.Tests/NPoco.Tests.csproj
        Dependency version bumps and whitespace.

Every other change in this fork lives in files that do not exist upstream:

    Directory.Build.targets
    NOTICE
    CHANGELOG.md
    src/NPoco.Abstractions/LegacyDateTime.cs
    src/NPoco.SqlServer/SqlServer2016Expression.cs
    src/NPoco.SqlServer/InListJson.cs
    src/NPoco.SqlServer/DatabaseTypes/SqlServer2016DatabaseType.cs
    test/NPoco.Tests/SqlServer2016ExpressionTests.cs
    test/NPoco.Tests/FluentSql/FluentSqlMarkerColumnTests.cs

These add OPENJSON-based IN clause generation for SQL Server 2016 and later,
used only when SqlServer2016DatabaseType is selected, and the LegacyDateTime
marker type.
